  "label": "general internet audience",
  "description": "The meme is designed for a broad online audience familiar with 9/11 history and dark humor tropes, likely targeting individuals who engage with internet memes, particularly those who appreciate or are exposed to edgy, controversial, or shock-value content. The target community includes users who may find the juxtaposition of a solemn memorial scene with a grotesque, dehumanizing joke amusing or provocative, even if it is offensive. The meme relies on cultural knowledge of the 9/11 attacks and the visual symbolism of the Twin Towers to deliver its message, so the audience must be aware of this context to fully comprehend the joke — or its intended shock value. The humor is rooted in dark humor, which is often consumed by internet communities that value provocative or boundary-pushing content.",
